# Which rd-api integration test binaries a change needs at branch level (RD-120-58).
#
# Read by rd_api_test_demands in scripts/lib/scope.sh. One row per line:
#
#     <extended regex over a changed path>   <binaries under crates/rd-api/tests/ | all | ->
#
# Every row whose regex matches a changed path contributes its binaries; `all` means every
# batch, `-` means none (the path is covered elsewhere). A row whose binaries start with `+`
# only adds them: it does not count as a mapping, so a path that matches nothing else still
# falls back to every binary. The rules around the table:
#
#   * A changed test file selects itself: crates/rd-api/tests/<name>.rs and tests/mcp/ -> mcp;
#     crates/rd-api/tests/common/ selects every binary.
#   * A changed path under crates/rd-api/, crates/rd-core/ or crates/rd-db/migrations/ that NO
#     row matches selects every binary. Where the mapping is not clear, the answer is the wide
#     one, never a guess; leaving a file out of this table is how to say "not clear".
#   * Any other crate selects no binary, as before RD-120-58: its own tests and one level of
#     reverse dependencies cover it at branch level, and --full runs everything.
#
# How a row is derived: from the routes a test binary requests (`/api/v1/<area>`) and the
# handler, service and route modules that serve them. Areas the tests reach from everywhere —
# settings, the router, auth, errors, DTOs, OpenAPI — select every binary. scope_matrix walks
# every route's policy and mcp drives the handlers through every tool, so any handler or route
# change selects both. check.sh refuses a row that names a binary which does not exist, and a
# binary that no row names: a new test file needs its row here.

# --- everything: the router, the shared types, settings -------------------------------------
^crates/rd-api/(Cargo\.toml|build\.rs)$                                                   all
^crates/rd-api/src/(lib|handlers|error|error_codes|dto|auth|scope_policy|client|trace_context|static_assets|event_stream)\.rs$   all
^crates/rd-api/src/openapi/                                                               all
^crates/rd-api/src/routes/(mod|config|system)\.rs$                                        all
^crates/rd-api/src/(config_handlers|setup_handlers)\.rs$                                  all
^crates/rd-core/(Cargo\.toml|build\.rs)$                                                  all
^crates/rd-core/src/(lib|error|ids|event|settings|download)\.rs$                          all
^crates/rd-db/migrations/                                                                 all

# --- every route, every MCP tool -------------------------------------------------------------
^crates/rd-api/src/(.*_handlers\.rs|routes/)                                              + scope_matrix mcp
^crates/rd-api/src/mcp/                                                                   mcp
# The page mcp::coverage::doc_tests include_str!s: a library test, and rd-api --lib always runs.
^crates/rd-api/mcp-coverage\.md$                                                          -

# --- unit tests inside the library: `rd-api --lib` runs them ---------------------------------
^crates/rd-api/src/.*tests\.rs$                                                           -

